Extension API: put the GAME popup's ten save slots on the wire.

Adds `MSG_SAVE_SLOTS` (0x14), server -> client, sent on the FIELDS
subscription right after a FIELD_LIST whenever the game is on
SCREEN_GAME (8) with the Load or Save dialog up (`MOX::_screen_data`
2 or 3). Payload: uint8 screen_data, uint8 count (10), then per slot
int8 status, int8 game type, char[37] description, char[25] stardate,
char[25] date — the engine's own values from `_game_popup_fields`,
`MOX::_save_game_description`, `MOX::_save_game_stardates` and
`MOX::_save_game_dates`, so a client draws what the dialog draws,
formatting included.

Open fix 14 in doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md; fundament decision 60 is
why a client does not read SAVEn.GAM from a folder of its own.

